ity on you  and he gives you the transparent aura  set for free from shell qua we can get a  bunch of really useful items you'll need  the cat ring to traverse the pit in  majula easily but did you also know that  she gives you a pair of boots that help  with falling damage after you kill the  Rat King it's kind of annoying that she  only gives them to you right after you  really need them but they're not bad  also you get the covetous silver serpent  ring after purchasing 10,000 souls worth  items from millennia and moving on to  another NPC one of my favorites this is  Lenna grassed the blacksmith in majula  his face is identical to the one you  find on the arch stone in Demon Souls  the  one that depicts the king of the borough  is underground there's actually another  reference to demon souls in majula  or I think there is anyway you see this  map in the mansion it's in one of the  Demon Soul cinematic so I swear this  landmass off to the side almost  perfectly matches the map of drangleic  in majula but notice I call these things  references not links to that game from a  law point of view Dark Souls is a  completely different universe to Demon  Souls and this has been pointed out by  the devs multiple times that doesn't  mean you can't think of it as related in  your own head you can keep your own head  Canon but that's just what the devs have  officially said and that's pretty much  it  let me know how many you got out of 10  leave a like if you learned something  new but from this point on this video is  going to be a bit of an update video for  those of you who are interested this is  a chance to look at where we've been and  where we kind of need to go from here  it's almost like traveling to majula  after you beat a boss then warping out  to the next zone you need to conquer you  know it's almost poetic so let's start  with the videos I've made in the past my  prepare to cry series comes to mind  first there are some seriously  heart-wrenching stories in 